  "choices": {},
  "race": "gnome",
  "subrace": "rock_gnome",
  "class": "druid",
  "background": "soldier",
  "backstory": "He was once a celebrated tactician within the Ironbound Legion, a rock gnome whose mind for siegecraft and battlefield geometry was whispered to be unmatched. Known for his soft-spoken grace and impeccable manners, he treated even his enemies with a courtier’s respect, believing that a disciplined soul was the mark of a true warrior. However, his obsession with perfection led to the catastrophe at the Blackvale Crossing. A single, calculated risk—a misjudged structural weakness in a bridge intended to trap the enemy—resulted in the drowning of an entire battalion of his own kin. Consumed by the weight of a failure that would destroy his standing and his honor, he stripped himself of his rank and his very name, vanishing into the untamed wilds before the true cause of the tragedy could be uncovered.\n\nIn the crushing silence of the deep forests, he found a new philosophy to replace his shattered pride: the cold, unyielding hierarchy of the natural world. He observed that nature does not offer mercy, only the cold truth that the strong consume the weak to fuel the next cycle of life. He embraced the druidic arts not out of a love for the wild, but out of a desire to master the apex forces that had once humbled him. To him, the storm, the predator, and the earthquake are the ultimate soldiers, and he treats them with the same polite reverence he once gave his generals. He views his magic as a weapon of absolute efficiency, believing that in the grand design of the world, might is the only mandate that matters.\n\nNow a nameless wanderer, he carries himself with the quiet dignity of a man who has nothing left but his word and his power. He adventures to test his resolve and to ensure that his past remains buried beneath the earth he now commands. His honor is a brittle, desperate thing, an armor he wears to hide the rot of his secret shame. He is a companion of impeccable courtesy, always bowing before a fray and speaking with a gentle tongue, yet those who watch him closely see the flint in his eyes. He will never again be the weaker force in any conflict, and he will go to any length—no matter how ruthless—to ensure that the ghosts of Blackvale stay silent forever.",
  "alignment": "chaotic_neutral",
  "name": "joni",
